{
  "name": "Trellis: YouTube Analytics Sync",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Trellis: YouTube Analytics Sync\n\nScheduled workflow that pulls YouTube performance data back into Trellis.\n\n### What it does\n1. Reads live YouTube rows from `trellis_episode_publications` using your existing Trellis Supabase credential.\n2. Extracts the YouTube video id from `external_id` or `external_url`.\n3. Calls YouTube Data API for public totals like views/likes/comments.\n4. Calls YouTube Analytics API for daily rows: views, watch time, avg view duration, retention, subscribers.\n5. Updates an existing row or creates a new row in `trellis_youtube_daily_metrics`.\n\n### Setup\n1. Import this workflow into n8n.\n2. On all Supabase nodes, select your existing Trellis Hub Supabase credential.\n3. On **YouTube Video Stats** and **YouTube Daily Analytics**, select a Google OAuth2 credential with these scopes:\n   - `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.readonly`\n   - `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/yt-analytics.readonly`\n4. Run manually once. Then activate the workflow.\n\n### Google credential note\nYour current Trellis YouTube API credential may work if it has the read/analytics scopes. If it only has upload scope, create or reconnect a Google OAuth2 credential with the two scopes above.\n\n### Notes\n- YouTube Analytics is delayed. New uploads may show no rows for a day or two.\n- Existing older publish rows may only have `external_url`; this workflow can extract ids from `youtu.be/...`, `watch?v=...`, and `/shorts/...` URLs.\n- The Trellis UI reads the same table and will fill in automatically after rows are written.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 700
      },
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        120,
        -460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 24
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "Daily Schedule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        180,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "return [{ json: {\n  lookback_days: 30,\n  publication_limit: 75\n} }];"
      },
      "name": "Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        400,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "row",
        "operation": "getAll",
        "tableId": "trellis_episode_publications",
        "returnAll": false,
        "limit": "={{ $('Config').item.json.publication_limit }}",
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "platform",
              "condition": "eq",
              "keyValue": "youtube"
            },
            {
              "keyName": "status",
              "condition": "eq",
              "keyValue": "live"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "name": "Fetch Live YouTube Publications",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.supabase",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        620,
        260
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "supabaseApi": {
          "id": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_HUB_SUPABASE_CREDENTIAL",
          "name": "Supabase account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "const cfg = $('Config').item.json;\nconst rows = $input.all().map(item => item.json).filter(Boolean);\n\nfunction extractVideoId(row) {\n  if (row.external_id && /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}$/.test(String(row.external_id))) return String(row.external_id);\n  const url = String(row.external_url || row.response?.youtube_url || row.response?.url || '');\n  const patterns = [\n    /youtu\\.be\\/([A-Za-z0-9_-]{11})/,\n    /[?&]v=([A-Za-z0-9_-]{11})/,\n    /\\/shorts\\/([A-Za-z0-9_-]{11})/,\n    /\\/embed\\/([A-Za-z0-9_-]{11})/,\n    /([A-Za-z0-9_-]{11})/\n  ];\n  for (const pattern of patterns) {\n    const match = url.match(pattern);\n    if (match) return match[1];\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nfunction isoDate(date) {\n  return date.toISOString().slice(0, 10);\n}\n\nconst now = new Date();\nconst end = new Date(Date.UTC(now.getUTCFullYear(), now.getUTCMonth(), now.getUTCDate() - 1));\nconst minStart = new Date(end);\nminStart.setUTCDate(minStart.getUTCDate() - Math.max(1, Number(cfg.lookback_days || 30)) + 1);\n\nconst jobs = [];\nfor (const row of rows) {\n  const videoId = extractVideoId(row);\n  if (!videoId || !row.episode_id || !row.id) continue;\n  const published = row.published_at ? new Date(row.published_at) : minStart;\n  const publishedDate = Number.isNaN(published.getTime()) ? minStart : published;\n  const start = new Date(Math.max(minStart.getTime(), Date.UTC(publishedDate.getUTCFullYear(), publishedDate.getUTCMonth(), publishedDate.getUTCDate())));\n  const safeStart = start.getTime() > end.getTime() ? end : start;\n  jobs.push({ json: {\n    publication_id: row.id,\n    episode_id: row.episode_id,\n    youtube_video_id: videoId,\n    external_url: row.external_url || `https://youtu.be/${videoId}`,\n    start_date: isoDate(safeStart),\n    end_date: isoDate(end)\n  } });\n}\n\nreturn jobs;"
      },
      "name": "Build Video Jobs",
